From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: explorer: toolbar arrows drawn on whole pixels, their heads symmetric

David: the Sort button's up and down arrows are not symmetrical, "one side
of each arrow is wrong". Drawn as lines at 16 pixels, one arm of every small
arrowhead came out a pixel longer than the other -- Up, Back and Forward too.
Straight arrows are now filled on whole pixels of the 16-unit grid: a
one-unit shaft and a head of mirrored diagonal steps.

Gate: make test-explorer-glyphs (the Up and Sort heads mirror about their
shafts).
--- a/programs/explorer/fileexplorer.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/fileexplorer.c
@@ -385,6 +385,33 @@
     return TRUE;
 }
 
+/* Stained Glass OS: a straight arrow drawn on whole pixels of the 16-unit
+ * grid -- a one-unit shaft and a head of mirrored diagonal steps -- so both
+ * sides of its head are the same (drawn as lines, one arm of every small
+ * head came out a pixel longer: David, "one side of each arrow is wrong").
+ * dir: 0 up, 1 down, 2 left, 3 right; c is the shaft's column (or row). */
+static void arrow_px(GpGraphics *g, GpBrush *b, int x, int y, float s, int dir, int c, int tip, int tail, int arm)
+{
+    int k, lo = min(tip, tail), len = abs(tail - tip) + 1, sign = (dir == 0 || dir == 2) ? 1 : -1;
+
+    if (dir <= 1) GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + c * s, y + lo * s, s, len * s);
+    else GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + lo * s, y + c * s, len * s, s);
+    for (k = 1; k <= arm; k++)
+    {
+        int along = tip + sign * k;
+        if (dir <= 1)
+        {
+            GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + (c - k) * s, y + along * s, s, s);
+            GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + (c + k) * s, y + along * s, s, s);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + along * s, y + (c - k) * s, s, s);
+            GdipFillRectangle(g, b, x + along * s, y + (c + k) * s, s, s);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
